OL,3,GNEWSAHousekeeper cleared of stealing
OL,4,Aprincess's jewels
OL,5,
OL,6,FA housekeeper has been cleared of
OL,7,Fstealing jewellery from the central
OL,8,FLondon home of a Jordanian princess.
OL,10,FPrincess Firyal Irshaid, 81, left the
OL,11,FUK during the Covid-19 pandemic in
OL,12,F2020. While she was away, part of her
OL,13,Fjewellery collection was taken and put
OL,14,Fup for sale at an auction house.
OL,16,FMaria Virgelina Taborda Henao, 71, who
OL,17,Fworked for the princess for 11 years,
OL,18,Fwas accused of stealing the items after
OL,19,Fbeing left to look after the Belgravia
OL,20,Fproperty. She was cleared of a charge
OL,21,Fof theft by employee by jurors at
OL,22,FSouthwark Crown Court.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
